# Product features and pricing

New Bronze listings are stored in
`data/collections/<category>/<market>/products/<source_key>/<product_id>/`.
Each website/storefront has a parent directory. Collection, verification,
processing and local evidence export support this layout; existing flat archives
remain readable and retain their stored history paths. The existing UK chocolate
corpus has also been physically grouped by website, with archive paths updated
directly and source evidence preserved. See the
[collection import contract](plugins/category-research/skills/category-research/references/import-contract.md).

The latest [retailer median refit](docs/data/analysis/retailer-median-training.md#refit-with-the-published-current-price-target)
uses the published current-price contract and all 2,134 eligible Gold rows.
Displayed prices and matching edible weights produce 630 GBP/100 g targets.
Missing variant IDs and population boundary values prevent a real fit. The
trainer preserves source evidence and saves exact input readiness artifacts.

Run the [Retailer Median Price Baseline](docs/data/analysis/retailer-median-training.md)
with `uv run python scripts/train_chocolate_retailer_median.py --gold-root <snapshot> --current-price-proxy`.
It has passed synthetic fitting validation. This study accepts displayed offers
and unverified tax metadata, with recorded limitations. Published historical OLS
and portable profiles retain their existing target contracts.

This repository studies how product features relate to prices across categories.
Chocolate sold in the UK is the current example. Preserve original information
and evidence before deriving an analytical schema or fitting a pricing model.

The retailer-facing Piece of Cake Pricing app helps category managers, buyers and
pricing teams inspect observed prices, product traits, assortment gaps and brand
positioning. It uses a layered terrain: observed GBP/100g, a disclosed trait-derived
demo score and one raw numeric leaf trait. Parent families organize navigation;
leaf categories or numeric bands supply colour layers. A price slider cuts the
cake vertically and shows the exposed layers at that price. A local product draft has
typed traits, a read-only score and a proposed-price slider. Image/text extraction
returns candidates for explicit review through OpenAI, a Codex bridge or direct
local Codex using ChatGPT OAuth sign-in. Local development defaults to direct
Codex; hosted provider setup remains pending.
The product form also predicts prices and explains five field contributions
using the published LightGBM synthetic fixture. It is labelled a demo; market
accuracy and real prediction intervals remain unvalidated.

