Run the web application with Node 24:

```sh
python3 -B scripts/fetch_web_pricing_model.py
cd apps/web
npm ci
npm run dev
```

Open `http://localhost:3000`. The deployment root is `apps/web`. Collection
exploration needs no external credentials; image/text extraction requires a
server-configured provider. The private web snapshot uses the published Gold inferred collection, pinned
in `apps/web/collection-dataset.json`, with 2,159 accepted trait additions and
preserved evidence. Refresh it with `uv run python -B scripts/build_web_snapshot.py`.
The upstream training and model workflow below retains its own versioning and
readiness. See the app README for current preview and validation.

The collection package bundles its [manifest](plugins/category-research/plugin.json)
and [skill](plugins/category-research/skills/category-research/SKILL.md), with a
Python CLI/API using the standard library. Packaging follows
https://agent-plugins.org/specification. Native installation and execution across
harnesses require verification.

Import a prepared collection from the repository root; this example writes to
`collections`:

```sh
python3 -B plugins/category-research/cli.py import --input <collection.json> --output collections --download-images --workers 4
```

The CLI reports the path to its run report and appends captures while preserving
earlier history. Read the [import contract](plugins/category-research/skills/category-research/references/import-contract.md)
for inputs, source/image preservation and archive/report semantics. Study records
retain broad product/variant indexes, arbitrary fields and raw prices, discovery
catalogues, source failures, cached text limitations, unavailable products and
ingredient gaps. They include their own guide and coverage; the earlier path is
`collections/chocolate/uk/README.md`. Listing counts describe selling sources and
require separate analysis to establish distinct products or market coverage.
The legacy `scripts/archive_product_sources.py` reproduces only the initial
exploratory sample of five products.

Collection `0.2.0` observes description, prices and availability by default.
Configure `collection_sections` for other source fields; observations describe
field presence and retain the complete original information.

The canonical chocolate workflow preserves raw evidence in
`data/collections/chocolate/uk` and builds one silver dataset in
`data/silver/chocolate/uk`. Silver combines deduplication within each seller,
typed schema/unit/vocabulary standardization, price normalization, evidence
review and model eligibility. Build directly from raw:

```sh
uv run --script scripts/build_chocolate_silver.py --archive-root data/collections --output data/silver/chocolate/uk
```

Silver preserves each shop's listings, separates brand from seller identity/role,
and links typed products to unchanged raw evidence through source listings and
aliases. See the [silver guide](docs/data/chocolate-silver.md) for the complete outputs
and seller partitions. Add `--reviews <reviews.json>` for
`chocolate-schema-reviews-1` decisions described in the
[schema guide](docs/data/chocolate-schema.md). That guide also owns `chocolate-schema-1` with 103 attributes, the 11 selected
predictors and model helpers.
The [plan](docs/lifecycle/plan.md) records current review, price/tax, extraction
and model validation gaps. Standalone deduplication, standardization and cleanup
CLIs serve compatibility and diagnostics.

The canonical chocolate build uses pandas 2.2.3. Direct Python callers need
that dependency installed; `uv sync --locked` installs it for development.
Runtime provenance and the table helper contribute to derived snapshot versions.

Inspect all-field coverage and exact selected-value frequencies in a downloaded
silver snapshot:

```sh
uv run --script scripts/analyze_chocolate_schema.py \
  --silver-root /path/to/downloaded/silver \
  --dataset-revision <immutable-40-character-dataset-commit> \
  --analysis-date <YYYY-MM-DD> \
  --output data/analysis/chocolate-schema-popularity.json
```

Replace the input path, commit and date with verified snapshot provenance.
Output must be outside the input directory. The helper verifies hashes and keeps
unknown/conflicting/review states separate. Counts describe collected seller
listings. See the [schema analysis guide](docs/data/chocolate-schema.md#inspect-field-coverage-and-value-frequencies)
and [publication receipt](docs/data/analysis/chocolate-pandas-publication-2026-10-03.json).

Analytical JSON contracts are authoritative in the
[Hugging Face dataset](https://huggingface.co/datasets/CoralLeiCN/rgc-collections)
under `contracts/chocolate/` and `contracts/category-processing/<category>/`.
Git retains human documentation and `dataset-contract.json` manifests with
immutable commit pins, per-file SHA-256 hashes and versions. Loaders download
missing pinned files into ignored caches and verify them before use. Cached runs
can be offline; the [dataset contract guide](docs/data/dataset-contracts.md) defines
cache and publication behavior.

The standalone processing package includes its runtime, five contract references,
stable seller UIDs, ledger, evidence batches, schema and processing skills, and model preparation.
Chocolate tracks 103 attributes; coffee demonstrates reuse with structured inputs.
These are optional examples. Processing `0.3.3` also generates five aligned
working contracts from an explicit category definition, including non-food
fields, units, quantity, currency and tax basis:

```sh
python3 -B plugins/category-processing/cli.py init-profile --input <category-definition.json> --output <new-profile-folder>
```

Bronze is the preserved raw-data layer: original collected records, source
artifacts and immutable capture history. Collection writes Bronze, processing
produces reviewed Silver, and Gold provides the training handoff.

The [fresh chocolate schema study](docs/data/schema-proposals/chocolate-bronze-reconstruction-2026-10-04.md)
reconstructs a 75-field proposal from Bronze and compares all 103 existing
attributes, with original evidence and explicit draft limitations.

Category processing starts with two inputs: available Bronze data and a
generated schema for the requested category/market. Use the dedicated
[category-schema skill](plugins/category-processing/skills/category-schema/SKILL.md)
to research raw captures and generate the missing initial catalog with evidence,
rationale and coverage gaps. Processing configures mappings/extraction, applies
the schema and finishes at reviewed Silver. Existing-schema refresh and extension
stay in processing maintenance. The subsequent
[Silver-to-Gold stage](plugins/category-processing/skills/category-processing/references/silver-to-gold.md)
owns model design and training-input preparation.

The current portable runtime still requires five files and writes legacy training
views; a new schema without the legacy model contract needs a runtime migration.
Do not invent model choices to begin processing. Published contracts remain in
the dataset with immutable references retained in Git.

Copy the entire package to use it independently of repository siblings or a
collection plugin installation. Run its workflow from the repository root:

```sh
python3 -B plugins/category-processing/cli.py process --archive-root data/collections --profile plugins/category-processing/profiles/chocolate --output data/silver/category-processing/chocolate/uk
python3 -B plugins/category-processing/cli.py summarize --silver-root data/silver/category-processing/chocolate/uk --output data/review-packets/chocolate/uk
```

The [portable guide](docs/data/category-processing.md) and package references cover
versions, review examples, outputs and mapping changes. Processing rebuilds fully;
the ledger reports input/rule changes. The harness maintains mappings within the
current task using evidence, versioned diffs, tests and impact review. Incremental processing caches,
external dispatch and scheduling are future work. The downstream compatibility
`prepare-model` helper requires reviewed eligible rows and at least two families,
and writes frozen inputs and an encoder; it does not create Parquet Gold. Current chocolate inputs are ineligible; regression fitting and model
validation remain future work. The original chocolate CLI keeps its established versions.

Structural discovery records unconfigured raw fields in `discovered-fields.jsonl`
and generates `schema-extension-review.md`. Keep hypotheses and decisions in
durable proposals linked to this evidence; see the initial
[seller review metrics](docs/data/schema-proposals/seller-review-metrics.md) and
[selling plan terms](docs/data/schema-proposals/selling-plan-terms.md) proposals.
The [standing maintenance decision](docs/decisions/agent-led-schema-maintenance.md)
allows supported local schema, mapping and parser changes without user approval.
When a schema changes, finish implementation and validation, present a detailed
release summary and wait for user review before its Hugging Face commit.

Use the locked development environment for pytest and Ruff, then run the
documentation guard under the policy:

On macOS, install the native OpenMP runtime with `brew install libomp` before
running the LightGBM trainers or the complete test suite. The Python dependency
lock does not install this system library; without it, LightGBM cannot load
`libomp.dylib` during test collection.

```sh
uv sync --locked
python3 -B scripts/fetch_contracts.py --all
uv run pytest
uv run ruff check .
python3 -B scripts/check_documentation.py
```

Use `python3 -B scripts/fetch_contracts.py --all --offline` to verify populated
caches. Runtime processing uses the standard library; pytest and Ruff are
development dependencies.

The [validation workflow](.github/workflows/validation.yml) runs checks on pull
requests and pushes. The lifecycle plan records verification and limitations.

Keep raw collection evidence and its verified text exports as local files under
[data specification section 3.1.1](docs/data/spec.md#311-public-dataset-publication-policy).
Exports preserve original product records, text/HTML/JSON, histories, catalogues,
discovery/run evidence and coverage in losslessly compressed category/market
bundles with a product JSONL index and manifests. Images and HTTP transfer caches
remain in the full raw archive, with omission metadata in the text export.
Build and inspect the local export without network access:

```sh
python3 -B scripts/publish_collections.py
```

The exporter discovers all studies under `data/collections/` and writes ignored
files under `data/huggingface-export/`. Use `--collections-root <directory>` and
`--output <directory>` for a shared local archive and a separate output root.
The JSON report records `export_bytes`. The former `--upload`, `--repo-id` and
`upload_export` interfaces reject raw publication before any side effect.

Hugging Face retains separately published Silver, Gold, analysis, model artifacts
and analytical contracts. Silver source-listings remain published by the user's
explicit choice. `scripts/publish_contracts.py` publishes contracts with immutable
reference manifests and preserves other current dataset files. Published Silver
requires separate evidence of review and model readiness. The public default
loader selects the existing Gold training table following raw index removal;
its `train` split name is a loader convention. The
[local storage receipt](docs/data/analysis/chocolate-local-raw-storage-2026-10-03.json)
records verified local source preservation and the remote removal. Follow the
[dataset contract guide](docs/data/dataset-contracts.md) and the
[schema release review](docs/decisions/agent-led-schema-maintenance.md#review-before-a-hugging-face-commit)
for analytical publication.

Original dataset reference: https://github.com/coveooss/SIGIR-ecom-data-challenge

## Gold, experimental training and product families

The [Gold guide](docs/data/chocolate-gold.md) defines immutable Parquet training snapshots, provenance and user-directed bulk review. Build and train with the locked development environment:

```sh
uv run python -B scripts/build_chocolate_gold.py --silver-root data/silver/chocolate/uk --output data/gold/chocolate/uk
uv run python -B scripts/train_chocolate_model.py --gold-root data/gold/chocolate/uk/<gold-version> --output data/models/chocolate/uk --group bar
```

Curated inference decisions can also be packaged in a separate immutable
[Gold inferred bundle](docs/data/chocolate-gold.md#build-a-separate-inferred-export).
It preserves full Silver records and the decision/source audit. Its version 1
`training/` child retains historical storage and source review flags; the current
Gold loader exposes every candidate for the selected study.

The raw-to-Silver builder includes reviewed family mappings from the [registry](reviews/chocolate/README.md), with `--family-mappings` overrides and grouped Codex review packets. The current chocolate study uses collected displayed prices as its regular-price proxy; independent regular-price and confirmed-tax evidence are not target requirements. The source Silver has family IDs on 402 candidates and zero eligible model inputs; the Gold loader includes all 2,134 candidates automatically, and current-price preparation derives 630 unit-price targets; the experimental OLS baseline has no real-data fit. [The published release](docs/data/analysis/gold-modeling-contract-release.md) records the verified contract publication and validation. Existing main features, discovery and proposed LightGBM/SHAP design remain available.


Gold now treats every row as part of the training population. New snapshots use
`chocolate-gold-population-1` / `chocolate-gold-arrow-3`, omit `model_eligible`
and `exclusion_reasons`, and contain one `training-data.parquet` table. To migrate
an existing snapshot, run `uv run python -B scripts/build_chocolate_gold.py
--gold-root /path/to/gold-snapshot --output data/gold/chocolate/uk`. The complete
parent and source evidence remain available. Historical snapshots also load as
the complete population without selection flags. Trainers still validate actual
model inputs. See [the Gold contract](docs/data/chocolate-gold.md#output-contract).

For the current chocolate study, append `--current-price-target` to the Gold
training command. It uses collected displayed prices as the target and records
promotion, tax and capture-date limitations. A separately verified regular price
is not required. Actual edible weight remains required for GBP per 100 g.
See [the specification](docs/data/chocolate-modeling-design.md#1-population-and-price-target)
and [project limitations](PROJECT.md#limitations).

## Independent LightGBM with brand

The [LightGBM with brand guide](docs/data/chocolate-lightgbm-with-brand.md) documents `scripts/train_chocolate_lightgbm.py`, frozen supermarket preparation, grouped family validation, native TreeSHAP, retailer calibration and immutable model runs. LightGBM 4.6.0 and SciPy 1.15.3 are pinned in the development lock. Its historical Gold attempts had zero eligible rows. The current published Gold contains 2,134 eligible rows; this frozen trainer still needs migration to the current-price policy and required shared fields. Fixture fitting is explicitly labeled, and real-data release and contract migration remain pending.

The refreshed all-eligible Gold is published at Hugging Face dataset revision
`95c5fbd0ab5fa9a41fa5333648321d95f16927a7`. The
[Gold guide](docs/data/chocolate-gold.md#published-all-eligible-training-snapshot)
records its exact download directory and
[checksum reference](schemas/chocolate/gold-dataset.json). It contains all
2,134 candidates in the training population and retains its complete original parent.
Use the current-price target policy when training this study.

## Independent LightGBM without brand

The [implementation guide](docs/data/analysis/lightgbm-without-brand-implementation.md)
documents the separate historical regular-price trainer, selected features,
family splits, calibration, TreeSHAP and immutable run loading. Use
`scripts/train_chocolate_model.py --model-id lightgbm_without_brand` with
`--gold-root` and `--working-contract`; prepare a configuration with
`--prepare-working-contract` and declare an evidenced price window. Its module
is `scripts/train_chocolate_lightgbm_without_brand.py`. The integrated lock
uses SciPy 1.15.3, matching the with-brand trainer.

The [published synthetic fixture](https://huggingface.co/datasets/CoralLeiCN/rgc-collections/tree/bb1c9de580c64cc13aac62b352d58704fe2dd60e/model/lightgbm_without_brand/fixtures/model-run-643f7148c9f44c42e5f42212)
retains its original source and SciPy 1.16.2 lock for exact reproduction. It
establishes synthetic implementation behavior only. This trainer requires
explicit migration before fitting the current-price study. Follow
[model maintenance](docs/model-maintenance.md) for Hugging Face artifacts and
Git publication receipts.

The independent [Hedonic Price Benchmark Without Brand](docs/data/analysis/hedonic-without-brand-implementation.md) is implemented under an explicit local working policy. Run `uv run python scripts/train_chocolate_model.py --model-id hedonic_without_brand --gold-root <snapshot> --working-contract <policy> --group bar`. Its numerical fixtures exercise family weighting, grouped selection, calibration and artifact integrity. This session's historical regular-price Gold rebuild has 2,134 candidates and zero eligible rows. Its fixture is published with synthetic status; no real hedonic fit or release is established. The newer current-price study retains its separate target and Gold identity.

The separate [matched retailer diagnostic](docs/data/chocolate-matched-retailer.md)
uses `uv run python scripts/train_chocolate_model.py --model-id matched_retailer
--gold-root <immutable-gold> --working-contract <local-contract> --group bar`.
It fits exact-variant and retailer fixed effects with family weighting and
uncertainty. The local working contract and matching evidence are explicit.
The published Gold has 2,134 eligible candidates and 630 current-price targets,
but every exact variant ID is missing, so the attempt saves readiness artifacts.
It provides matched-assortment contrasts without new-product prediction support.

When the calling task explicitly confirms all Gold candidates as verified, append
`--verified-gold-candidates` to the matched-retailer command. This uses existing
Gold directly, records the verification basis and preserves stored metadata.
For the historical regular-price configuration, missing prices and exact identities prevent a fitted
matched comparison. See the [direct Gold path](docs/data/chocolate-matched-retailer.md#task-authorized-gold-verification).

The Gold loader accepts verified `chocolate-gold-bulk-eligibility-1` snapshots
through embedded-parent integrity checks. The [matched refresh command](docs/data/chocolate-matched-retailer.md#refresh-from-promoted-gold)
uses the supplied newer promoted Gold directly and binds its copied contracts
in an explicit local configuration. Its historical regular-price attempt found
missing regular targets and exact variant IDs.

The current study now permits collected current/displayed GBP prices as an
explicit proxy target. Add `--current-price-proxy` when preparing a fresh matched
working configuration. The [current-price guide](docs/data/chocolate-matched-retailer.md#current-price-study-policy)
documents source preservation, positive candidate edible weight matching price
quantity, promotion/tax limitations and the remaining exact-variant requirement.
Run `python3 -B scripts/fetch_contracts.py --current-price` to cache the published
target overlay; `--all` now verifies or fetches all four contract sets. The current
matched design binds this overlay offline and derives 630 targets from the
2,134-row Gold snapshot. Missing exact variant IDs prevent a matched fit.

## Refit LightGBM from inferred Gold

All Gold candidates enter training as eligible under
`chocolate-gold-training-all-rows-2`; original source decisions remain
provenance. Inferred Gold joins typed product cells with unchanged source
prices for the current displayed-price study. With the verified snapshot and
pinned contracts cached locally, run:

```sh
uv sync --locked
python3 -B scripts/fetch_contracts.py --all --offline
uv run python scripts/train_chocolate_model.py \
  --model-id lightgbm_without_brand \
  --gold-root data/gold-inferred/chocolate/uk/gold-inferred-5b539b9c4adbb011a40d7792
```

The [refit record](docs/data/analysis/lightgbm-without-brand-inferred-refit.md)
links the published experimental run, selected features, family holdout results and
limitations. Missing price, mass or family grouping still restrict numerical
use. The 55-row Waitrose fit has no calibrated intervals or market-release
claim. See the [Gold guide](docs/data/chocolate-gold.md) for admission, immutable
source verification and inferred-wrapper provenance.
